      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"The notion of 'Indian' governance is little more than an exercise in benevolent paternalism. As civilized statesmen, we have merely taken upon ourselves the protection and guidance of a people swayed by unfettered savagery and superstition, their cyclical chronicles devoid of logic and reason. It is our duty, our sacred obligation, to educate, transmit Western tenets, and constrain the tribal impulses that threaten the advancement of this fair subcontinent. Abandonment to ourselves would only incite bankruptcy and tantrums, a besmirched legacy awaiting the refined expertise of the British.\"",
